title: September 2022

@september_2022
# prose-audit: Grade A — The winter price shock is grounded in households, services, firms and energy ownership, with four distinct settlements and candid factional consequences.
title: The price of winter
face-image: img/poland/events/turow-mine-2021.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.energy_2022_done = 1;
Q.inflation = Math.max(Number(Q.inflation) || 0, 17.2);
Q.energy_security -= 4;
Q.household_security -= 4;
Q.war_fatigue += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 9;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 10;
Q.news_headline =
    "Energy prices turn solidarity into a distributional fight";
!}

= September 2022 — Who absorbs the shock?

Russian supply cuts and replacement purchases move through state utilities into
the bills of households, hospitals, schools and small firms. PiS promises caps,
KO attacks the government's energy record and Konfederacja treats every levy
and climate rule as part of the same failure.

Lewica must choose who receives a universal guarantee, who pays for it and
whether this winter accelerates public transition or suspends it. Every answer
protects somebody first and leaves somebody else carrying the uncertainty.

- @sep22_cap
- @sep22_public
- @sep22_target
- @sep22_deregulate

@sep22_cap
title: Cap household prices and levy extraordinary profits
subtitle: Give every household a clear ceiling and make energy windfalls finance it.
on-arrival: energy_2022_stance = "Universal cap"; household_policy_pressure += 6; labor_credibility += 4; budget_promises += 2; left_economic_position -= 4; pis_economic_position -= 2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "A windfall-funded cap becomes the social opposition line"

Tenant groups, unions and pensioners receive a number they can plan around. The
windfall levy lets Lewica say who should finance the guarantee rather than
placing its entire cost in an unspecified future budget.

Large energy firms dispute what counts as an extraordinary profit, and the
promise is expensive if the levy falls short. PiS begins borrowing the cap
while resisting our account of who should pay.

- @sep22_reparations: Turn to the reparations report


@sep22_public
title: Pair short relief with public-energy investment
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The programme cannot be assembled.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; household_policy_pressure += 3; climate_policy_pressure += 3; administrative_reform_pressure += 5; public_trust += 3; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Relief and transition enter one costed programme"

The policy team joins short-term relief to insulation, municipal heat and
public renewable investment, with costs and delivery offices named. Climate
organisers can defend the emergency package without pretending winter bills
will wait for new infrastructure.

The programme consumes the organisation's remaining capacity and offers less
immediate simplicity than a universal cap. Its reward is a route that does not
repeat the same crisis next year.

- @sep22_reparations: Turn to the reparations report


@sep22_target
title: Target help at vulnerable households and public services
subtitle: Concentrate scarce support and reopen the Left's argument over universalism.
on-arrival: household_policy_pressure += 4; health_policy_pressure += 2; public_sector_support += 2; left_economic_position += 1; razem_dissent += 3; barons_dissent -= 2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Targeted relief limits cost and reopens universalism"

Hospitals, schools and households below a clear income threshold receive the
first guarantee. The narrower package is cheaper and directs money toward the
people least able to absorb another bill.

Families just above the line become the opposition's counterexample, and Razem
warns that means testing can turn a universal energy crisis into another queue
for proof of poverty.

- @sep22_reparations: Turn to the reparations report


@sep22_deregulate
title: Suspend climate rules and cut energy taxes
subtitle: Lower the visible burden quickly by moving onto Konfederacja's economic terrain.
on-arrival: climate_policy_pressure -= 6; left_economic_position += 5; left_right_score += 4; market_liberal_support += 9; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; rural_support += 1; progressives_dissent += 9; labor_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 7; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Emergency deregulation moves the debate onto Konfederacja's ground"

Fuel sellers, small firms and some rural households welcome an immediate cut
in taxes and compliance costs. Lewica gains access to voters who believe every
other party has made energy deliberately expensive.

The programme gives up revenue and climate safeguards without controlling the
wholesale price. Konfederacja claims authorship, while progressives, labour and
Razem confront a Left leadership using the emergency to adopt its opponent's
settlement.

- @sep22_reparations: Turn to the reparations report


@sep22_reparations
# prose-audit: Grade C — The figure, its legal weakness and the domestic purpose are stated plainly with three usable Lewica lines; the surviving claimants are named as a category rather than as people.
title: Six point two trillion
subtitle: Warsaw formally demands war reparations from Berlin
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-kaczynski-2023.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.sep22_reparations_done = 1;
Q.german_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.german_relation) || 55) - 12
);
Q.public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "Poland formally demands 6.2 trillion złoty in war reparations from Germany";
!}

= September 2022 — A number with a domestic address

The parliamentary report is published on 1 September and the figure is **6.2
trillion złoty**. A diplomatic note follows. Berlin answers within days that
the question is legally closed and will not be reopened, which everybody in
Warsaw expected and several people in Warsaw wanted.

The losses were real and were never compensated, and most of the people who
suffered them are dead. The claim's legal position is weak — successive Polish
governments treated the matter as settled — and its political position is
excellent, three months into an energy crisis and a year out from an election.

It is therefore two things at once: an unanswerable moral account of what was
done to this country, and an instrument for turning a winter of bills into a
question about Germany.

[? if energy_2022_stance = "Universal cap": We have just spent the month
arguing about who pays for winter, which is precisely the argument this
announcement is designed to replace.?]
[? if eu_veto_stance = "Costed in delivery": We priced the 2020 veto in
hospitals and rail. The same method applies here and will be received far
worse, because this time the subject is the war.?]

- @rep22_survivors
- @rep22_refuse_frame
- @rep22_support

@rep22_survivors
title: Support the claim and demand the money reach surviving victims first
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Keeps the moral case and refuses to let it be spent on a campaign.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot staff a survivors' compensation proposal this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.reparations_stance = "Survivors first";
Q.civic_patriotism = (Number(Q.civic_patriotism) || 10) + 5;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.pensioner_support = (Number(Q.pensioner_support) || 0) + 4;
Q.social_patriot_support =
    (Number(Q.social_patriot_support) || 0) + 4;
Q.german_relation = (Number(Q.german_relation) || 43) + 3;
Q.labor_credibility = (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left backs the claim and asks who among the living would be paid";
!}

We support the account and attach the only question that makes it a policy
rather than a slogan: of the people alive today who were forced labourers,
camp survivors or children of the deportations, how many would receive
anything, when, and through which office.

The government has no answer, because the claim was never designed to produce
a payment. Survivors' organisations, which have been asking this since the
1990s, find themselves quoted in a national argument for the first time in
years.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@rep22_refuse_frame
title: Say the demand is a domestic instrument and take the consequences
subtitle: Accurate and the most expensive sentence available in September 2022.
on-arrival: {!
Q.reparations_stance = "Named as domestic instrument";
Q.german_relation = (Number(Q.german_relation) || 43) + 8;
Q.eu_relations = (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 45) + 4;
Q.public_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 3
);
Q.social_patriot_support = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.social_patriot_support) || 0) - 6
);
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) - 4;
Q.civic_patriotism = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.civic_patriotism) || 10) - 3
);
Q.konf_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left calls the reparations note an election document";
!}

We say it: the note was sent to a government that had already answered, in the
week the energy bills arrived, by a party that has held office for seven years
without filing it. That is not a claim being pursued. That is a claim being
used.

Being right about this is worth very little in September 2022. The clip runs
in every county where somebody's grandmother was deported, without the
sentence about the deportations, and our own patriotic organisers spend the
autumn defending a position they did not choose.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@rep22_support
title: Endorse the demand without conditions and move on
subtitle: The safe answer; it concedes the subject and the ownership of it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.reparations_stance = "Unconditional endorsement";
Q.civic_patriotism = (Number(Q.civic_patriotism) || 10) + 3;
Q.social_patriot_support =
    (Number(Q.social_patriot_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.german_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.german_relation) || 43) - 4
);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.media_capacity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) - 1
);
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left endorses the reparations claim and adds nothing to it";
!}

We vote for the resolution, say the losses were real, and decline to discuss
the arithmetic or the timing. It is defensible and it takes an afternoon.

The subject belongs to PiS for the rest of the parliament. Whenever it is
raised — and it is raised whenever something else is going badly — we are
listed among the parties that agreed and had nothing further to say.

- @poland_hub: Continue
